<div class="card">

<h2>6. Sea Breeze</h2>

<p>
During the day, land heats faster than water. Warm air over
the land rises, and cooler air from the sea moves toward the land.
</p>

<div class="formula">
Day → Sea → Land
</div>

<div class="success">
Sea breeze occurs mainly during the day.
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>7. Land Breeze</h2>

<p>
At night, land cools faster than water. Air over the sea is
relatively warmer and rises, while cooler air moves from land
toward the sea.
</p>

<div class="formula">
Night → Land → Sea
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>8. Black and Shiny Surfaces</h2>

<div class="grid">

<div class="mini">

<h3>Black / Dull Surface</h3>

<p>
Good absorber and good emitter of thermal radiation.
</p>

</div>

<div class="mini">

<h3>Shiny / Polished Surface</h3>

<p>
Poor absorber and poor emitter of thermal radiation;
good reflector.
</p>

</div>

</div>

<div class="warning">
This is why thermos flasks use reflective surfaces to reduce
radiative heat transfer.
</div>

</div>


<div class="card">

<h2>9. Greenhouse Effect — Basic Idea</h2>

<p>
Certain gases in Earth's atmosphere absorb and re-emit infrared
radiation, contributing to warming of the lower atmosphere and
surface.
</p>

<div class="info">
The greenhouse effect is a natural atmospheric phenomenon,
though increased concentrations of greenhouse gases can enhance it.
</div>

